This drug addict is going into shock!

82
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,280
All right, listen up!

83
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:39,360
Stay back or the priest gets it!

84
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:42,417
Careful, the druggies
awake and out of control!

85
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,330
Damn it!

86
00:06:43,413 --> 00:06:44,637
He cut me with those scissors!

87
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:46,697
Don't you point those fucking guns at me!

88
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:48,100
No way!

89
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:51,614
There ain't no way in hell
I'm gonna let you lock me up!

90
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:00,839
Requesting backup.

91
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:03,357
There's a hostage
situation at the hospital.

92
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:04,780
Hey, shit for brains!

93
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,617
What the hell did you just say?

94
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:09,540
Are you stupid, or do
you want this guy to die?

95
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,646
You really pissed me off now!

96
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:15,452
This fucking stone is about
to get stabbed because of you!

97
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:19,220
Earlier tonight, I saw shooting
stars in the sky above.

98
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,400
Three to be precise.

99
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:25,560
Just three, clearly
streaking across the sky.

100
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:29,220
May I ask where you came from?

101
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:33,060
Do you three have any idea
who it is you truly are?

102
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,230
Shit!

103
00:07:39,313 --> 00:07:40,277
The psycho stabbed him!

104
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,960
Wait a sec, that wasn't me!

105
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:43,000
No, it wasn't.

106
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:46,397
However, if you were to move
this blade another millimeter,

107
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:49,421
it would certainly sever
a vital nerve in my neck.

108
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:50,778
What a coincidence.

109
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:54,753
Fortunately, this stab wound
does not appear to be fatal.

110
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,040
What will you do?

111
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,278
It's your decision.

112
00:07:57,480 --> 00:08:00,186
Do you want to move the
scissors a bit or not?

113
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:02,460
But first, answer me this.

114
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,197
Do you believe in gravity?

115
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:08,237
Do you think there is a force that
draws certain individuals together?

116
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:10,957
Personally, this moment
has made me a believer.

117
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:13,317
However, you are not
capable of killing me.

118
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,820
You're here because my
gravitational pull led you to me.

119
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:21,017
Don't you see that you shouldn't be
wasting your energy on useless drugs?

120
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:24,629
No, you should be using your
energy on something much wiser.

121
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,820
Fuck this!

122
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:38,017
From the looks of things, where it
pertains to who your father really is,

123
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:40,394
The three of you were left in the dark,

124
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:42,780
but that won't last much longer.

125
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:56,685
Now that we've been brought together, you
will understand everything soon enough.

126
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,560
Thank you very much.

127
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:26,660
I'm fine.

128
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,220
Sorry to bother you.

129
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:29,440
This is nothing.

130
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:32,485
Just an old knee injury
from my carpentry days.

131
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:35,212
When it rains, my joints start to twinge.

132
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:37,380
When it rains, your knee hurts.

133
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:39,910
Sure does.

134
00:09:39,993 --> 00:09:42,058
Thanks for showing me some kindness.

135
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:46,636
Stop getting into random
stranger's business, Weather.

136
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:49,100
We're still fugitives, remember?

137
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,717
Our faces are blasted all over the news.

138
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,388
The geezer might report us.

139
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:57,777
Our best bet is to steal a car and
get the hell out of Dodge immediately.

140
00:09:57,860 --> 00:09:59,057
No stolen cars.

141
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,434
It'll be too easy for them to track us.

142
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,537
And then we'll never lose them.

143
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:05,897
Chasing the priest
would become impossible.

144
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,397
You're not suggesting we
take the bus, are you?

145
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:11,833
How long are we supposed to
wait till the next one comes?

146
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:13,200
Oh, hey, fellas.

147
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,097
You think I'm gonna take in the bus?

148
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:18,420
It won't be here for another hour.

149
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:21,217
How about I give you
boys a ride on my truck?

150
00:10:21,300 --> 00:10:23,457
You'll have to hop in the back, though.

151
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:26,217
Maybe it's because you
were so kind to me earlier.

152
00:10:26,300 --> 00:10:28,241
But I'm feeling better than ever.

153
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:33,380
The pain on my knees was awful moments
ago, but it's miraculously gone. Come on!

154
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,501
The sky feels so refreshing, too!

155
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:45,920
Weather forecast.

156
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,040
Call it luck.

157
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:53,398
We should take his offer, Anastasia.

158
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:10,480
So how's Jolene getting around right now?

159
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:13,040
She is still safe, isn't she?

160
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:15,820
Jolene is currently heading north.

161
00:11:16,240 --> 00:11:17,475
Of that, I'm certain.

162
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:21,500
At any rate, we need to
be heading north as well.

163
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:27,797
There's a famous theme
park in the city up north.

164
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:29,056
You ever been there?

165
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:30,814
