could it be an enemy
dive or drive i got it

172
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:15,940
You sure i still see something darting
around yeah well i got this one for sure

173
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:19,960
But what the hell is this thing

174
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:36,082
Beyond the alert weather forecast
the stand user must be somewhere

175
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:40,617
There's zero chance this old man's
the stand user there's no reason

176
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:44,117
to show up the way he did He could
have just attacked us from anywhere.

177
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:46,977
If it's not him, it must be
someone else in the area.

178
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:49,437
Just like you're able to
sense where Jolene is going.

179
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:51,937
Maybe the priest can
sense us getting closer

180
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:54,637
and is sending his lackeys to
stop us from getting to him.

181
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:55,977
Now who the hell are you?

182
00:12:56,060 --> 00:12:56,890
Tell us!

183
00:12:56,973 --> 00:12:58,317
You really shouldn't do that.

184
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,597
Please stop choking me.

185
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:00,510
It hurts.

186
00:13:00,593 --> 00:13:03,812
You're going to make children
all over the world very sad.

187
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,320
Is that so?

188
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:07,978
For real though, they can't breathe.

189
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:09,397
Come on, give it a rest.

190
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:11,400
Seriously, man, I'm begging you.

191
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:14,437
There's another little bastard
hiding on this truck, too.

192
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,344
Yeah, you two working together?

193
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:17,640
Uh, nuh-uh.

194
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:18,720
I work alone.

195
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:24,800
My bad, man.

196
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,300
So sorry about that.

197
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:28,186
I swear it wasn't on purpose.

198
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:30,000
You son of a...

199
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:33,497
Honestly, my nose just
grows on its own sometimes.

200
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:35,756
You know, it's sort of like a reflex.

201
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:38,837
See, whenever I tell a lie, my
nose gets all long and junk.

202
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:41,160
And I just lied straight to your face.

203
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:45,580
But what I told you wasn't exactly
a complete lie. So basically,

204
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:47,557
I might not be working with somebody,

205
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:50,377
but that doesn't mean that
I'm alone necessarily.

206
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:51,290
Yeah.

207
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:53,610
Oh!

208
00:13:53,693 --> 00:13:54,523
Hey, check it out!

209
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:56,097
This proves I'm not lying.

210
00:13:56,180 --> 00:14:00,040
You believe me now, right?
Ow! Shit! What are you?

211
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:02,515
Didn't I say to stop being so violent?

212
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:07,317
It feels kind of weird saying this about
myself, but I think I'm a pretty good guy.

213
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:09,871
I'm definitely nice to children, at least.

214
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:13,747
Actually, I might have been your
friend when you were younger.

215
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:15,140
Yeah, that's right.

216
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:19,357
Speaking of friends, I think the seven
of them are hiding around here somewhere.

217
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:22,560
I saw three of the seven
guys a minute ago. See?

218
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:25,762
Someone's been snacking
on that apple over there.

219
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:31,317
Hey, Weather, you seeing this?

220
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,929
What the fuck is going on?

221
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:40,697
Just so you know, that
apple isn't poisonous!

222
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:41,900
It's okay to eat.

223
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:44,637
Yeah, but the one Snow
White ate was poisonous.

224
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:46,197
No, she didn't actually eat it.

225
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,697
She choked on a piece of it.

226
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:49,956
So technically, she didn't digest it.

227
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:54,224
But I mean, who'd eat an apple
from an old lady they didn't know?

228
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:57,977
Even on Valentine's Day, we're careful
about the chocolates we put in our mouths.

229
00:14:58,060 --> 00:14:59,657
Although it's that
carelessness of hers that

230
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:02,740
